  "steps": [
    "## Prep",
    "Divide the beef into 6 equal portions and roll each into a ball. Compress each ball by passing it between your hands, then chill uncovered in the fridge.",
    "Whisk all the special sauce ingredients in a small bowl until smooth. Refrigerate until serving.",
    "## Cook",
    "Heat a large cast iron griddle or skillet over medium-high heat. Add the oil, and when it shimmers toast the buns cut side down until deep golden. Set aside.",
    "Season the tops of 3 beef balls with salt and put them on the hot griddle. If using onions, pile them on top of each ball. Press each firmly with a heavy burger press to about 6 mm thick.",
    "Cook about 1 minute, until deeply golden and lacy at the edges. Season the other side, flip, and cook about 30 seconds, adding oil as needed. Repeat with the remaining 3 balls.",
    "Turn off the heat. Put American cheese on 3 patties and cheddar on the other 3. Cover to melt, then stack the patties, alternating the cheese.",
    "## Assemble",
    "Put a patty stack on each toasted bun and top with pickle chips, ketchup, mustard and special sauce. Serve immediately."
  ],
